WEBVTT

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
kyou mo ashita mo HIMAKKUSU

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
gokazoku yonin de goippaku

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
EGIPUTO kidori de SUFINKUSU

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
AMERICA kibun de TEXAS

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
yoyuu SHAKUSHAKUPPE itsumo

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
funya funya de iruto

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.930
and your bitter face and bitter feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.930
nigamushi hara no mushi nahe nahe to

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
tettai shichau yo

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
watashi ha URUTORA RIRAKKUSU

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
SUTEKI ni muteki na RIRAKKUSU

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
hito aji chigau ze DERAKKUSU

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
I may be a little jumbled,

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
toccharakatte mo

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
yobarerya PAPAPAPAAAN!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
watashi ha itsudemo RIRAKKUSU

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
WABISABI kikasete DERAKKUSU

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
BIKKARI! KIKKARI! saeteru ATAMA PII! PII!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
Keep your eyes on me, okay?!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
watashi no KOTO dake mitete ne!

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.610
I'm Kurata Sana, a first-year in junior high.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.530
The amazing white bat, Babbit!

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:41.620
When you do things you must have a beginning and an end.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:45.460
My best friend here in New York,
Naozumi-kun.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.580
You're in the way!
Get out of my face!

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.380
How can you say something like that?

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.970
Because he really is in the way.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:01.890
Ah...

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:06.680
My trumpet is in the bedroom, right?

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:26.750
Should We Go Back?
Will We Go Back?

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.090
He's only a child.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:37.050
Because of that, he thinks dreaming about it is enough.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.340
Well, he's wrong!

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.180
Sana-chan.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.180
Hmm?

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.480
To Central Park...

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:33.690
Okay.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:52.670
Back there, that person said she was my mother.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.670
It feels funny.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:03.260
She was just taking advantage of me.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:09.930
Hamilton-san also said that because I am a semi-famous child star in Japan...

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:14.770
I was taken advantage of...

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:16.190
Isn't that right?

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:22.570
But... I think of everybody at the Kamura Academy as my family.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:27.160
I never really thought about living with my real parents.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:31.370
I was already abandoned once by my mother, so this is the second time, not the first.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:37.170
Sana-chan.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.880
Why are you crying, Sana-chan?

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.180
Sana-chan...

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.310
Please don't cry.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:11.160
I know it seems harsh, but because this is the second time... It's really nothing...

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.660
...don't let go...

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:18.960
Naozumi-kun, I'm here.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.460
I'm here, close to you.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:26.470
Always, always I'll be here for you.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:29.470
Won't I, Naozumi-kun?

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.680
Sana-chan...

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:59.580
Morning at
the Hamilton's

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:58.370
I'm Sicil. Sicil Hamilton.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:05:59.750
You can't fool me.

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:03.880
- Good morning, Sicil.
- Good morning.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.970
Good morning, Papa, Mama.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:08.890
It wasn't a dream.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:15.680
It's strange, but pleasant to have everyone here for breakfast.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.690
It's not bad, this kind of thing.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:20.690
From now on, we can always have meals together.

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:22.570
You're right.

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:25.480
This really isn't a dream!

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.370
I'm happy for you, Sicil.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:37.830
That guy... why?

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.670
Leaving, because Naozumi-kun is exhausted?

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:41.580
Are you okay?

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:50.220
New York, huh?

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:55.180
Why did we come here in the first place?

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:59.190
If we hadn't come to this town...

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:02.770
Naozumi-kun wouldn't have had to go through something like this.

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:06.190
Was this such a good idea?

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:22.460
Sana-chan, let's go to New York.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:25.800
We need to escape, both of us.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.260
Naozumi-kun was right there to back me up.

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:31.680
That time...

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:37.810
He rescued me when I had my heart broken.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:42.400
Let's escape, together.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.560
This time, it's my turn...

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:46.980
...to rescue Naozumi-kun.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:49.320
Shall we go back?

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:52.990
What?

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:55.490
Want to go back? To Japan.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:56.950
Alright?

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.000
Sana-chan... but...

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:02.580
Don't even say you want to work instead.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:04.960
To be honest, I'm tired of working.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.090
And this time...

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:14.090
Things have been crazy since we got that letter asking us to work here.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:18.470
It's a big job, but we don't have to do it.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:22.390
You and I can still be anything we want!

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:27.190
Naozumi-kun, don't you think you're pushing yourself too much?

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:32.360
I guess so...

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:33.860
Thank you, Sana-chan.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:36.160
But, I'm alright.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:38.490
Because you're here to support me.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.790
Sana-chan, is it alright with you?

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:45.170
...to go back to Japan so soon?

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:54.380
Yeah... since I'll have to see them sooner or later...

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:55.590
Yes!

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:56.760
Okay.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:59.100
I gotcha. Shall we go home?

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:03.430
Bye-bye!
New York

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:01.390
Who are you?

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:02.850
Metropolitan!

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.480
Here, Papa.

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:09.690
Thank you, Sicil. They're very pretty.

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:12.570
Sicil.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:17.280
I'm sorry. Many painful things have happened because of the incident with Naozumi.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:18.490
No, it's alright.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:22.580
When I found out that Naozumi was my big brother, I was a bit shocked, but...

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:26.170
Sicil, I should have told you about this.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:27.580
It's okay.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:31.300
I'm going to go see Naozumi today.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.300
Sicil, what do you think about that?

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:34.880
It's fine with me.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.590
Is that so?

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:39.390
Naozumi is also my child.

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:42.680
I was thinking that Naozumi would be welcome to live together with us.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:43.470
I see.

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:46.690
Hey old man, are you really seriously considering that?

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:50.190
It's Sicil-chan...

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:59.450
Papa is very kind.
Mama is also very kind.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:02.280
But if Naozumi comes...

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:06.080
Naozumi will be able to dance, but I won't be able to.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.670
If Naozumi comes...

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:12.170
I got seats on today's flight!

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.380
This afternoon?

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:15.380
Then we don't have much time, do we?

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:16.260
Go home, go home...

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:18.300
I don't think Rei-kun heard us...

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:23.390
Asako, I'm home!

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:26.390
Welcome home, Rei!

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:31.270
The couple is happy!

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:33.690
Asako, I bet you were taking it easy, weren't you?

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:37.570
I was so lonely without you,
I had trouble eating!

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.780
You didn't eat? Don't do that, it's not good for you!

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:41.990
I'm sorry, Rei!

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:42.870
Asako...

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.290
...Asako...

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:46.370
My beloved, Asako!

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:48.790
Asako, Asako...

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:50.880
You are my family treasure...

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:53.380
You are so gentle...

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:54.960
You want to go back?!

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.670
Bernie.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:11:00.590
O-Oh, don't become a strange person like him.

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:01.970
Nyaaa...

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:04.680
When you came, I knew you would have to leave someday.

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:08.980
But still, it's so early...
it seems so sudden.

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:10.190
Bernie.

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:12.400
Here, take this.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.360
I know it's not much...

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:16.480
...but please use it.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:18.190
Sana, thank you.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:20.860
I don't have anything to give you, Bernie, but...

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:21.860
That's alright.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:24.070
I... that is...

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:28.790
We've been through many things since we came to New York, but...

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:31.290
Coming to New York...

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:34.170
I think it was really a good thing to have come...

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:36.460
And to have met you, Bernie.

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.170
Naozumi.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:40.090
I'm also glad I met you, Bernie!

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:42.260
I was also glad to have met you!

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.260
How do we say this?

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.470
Meeting you, Bernie,
was really a good thing.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:47.770
I'm so happy...

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:50.060
My heart's pounding all of a sudden.

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:52.270
Happy... I'm so happy...

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:56.570
Here, I'll give you my nail polish.

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:59.320
Bernie is a good person

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:59.190
I can't use it because I don't have any fingernails!

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:03.200
I see. Well, I must be going.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:05.490
He hasn't arrived at the office yet?

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:08.290
We should at least get in touch with Hamilton once before leaving.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.370
Shall I call him at his house?

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:12.000
Naozumi-kun.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.670
Don't worry, Sana-chan.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.460
I'll definitely get in touch with him.

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:16.380
Okay.

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:40.480
{parte b}

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:43.990
Babbit's Counting Song

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:43.570
Sing well!

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:46.570
1,2,1,2,3,7

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:49.490
"Seven", "seven", that's how you say "shichi" in English

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:52.500
In Japanese, you can also say "nana"

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:55.370
"Seven", "seven", that's how you say "shichi" in English

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:58.880
In Japanese, you can also say "nana"

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:01.460
What, today you only have that much?

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:07.300
I'll get it.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:08.390
Please excuse me.

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.680
Hello, this is the Hamilton residence.

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:13.680
Naozumi.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:14.980
S-Sicil.

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:19.690
Umm, is Hamilton-san there?

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.280
Papa?!

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:22.190
Papa...

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:26.360
He can't come right now.

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:28.780
I see...

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:32.080
Well, Sicil, it's sudden but...

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:34.580
We've decided to go back to Japan.

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:35.660
To Japan?!

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:39.080
We'll be leaving New York this afternoon.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:41.630
It's so sudden.

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:44.880
I know. It is...

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:49.180
Well, since we're going back to Japan, I was wondering if you could pass on the news.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.890
Sicil?

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:53.970
I understand.

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:57.600
But I'm glad I was able to hear your voice one last time.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.570
And also...

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:02.480
Hmm?

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:05.990
Sicil, listen.

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:11.660
Gary-san, Michelle-san, and you, Sicil, are all very important to me.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:16.000
I love you more than anybody.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.580
Do you understand, Sicil?

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:20.460
Naozumi, I...

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:21.670
Sicil?

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:22.800
Sana!

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:27.720
We were hoping to come see you before we go home, but I'm sorry we can't.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.470
But please come to visit us in Japan.

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.760
Take care of Ramsy-san for me, ok?

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:36.390
I don't really want to say this... Brad...

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:41.560
Still, take care of Maekibakaanbarinihototoki-san...

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:42.560
Who's that?

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:43.980
To tell the truth, it's Makubagyapan-san.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:46.860
Ooh... my name is Sana Kurata.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:49.570
You really can't say anything to be proud of, can you?

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:51.160
See you later, Sicil, take care.

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:53.280
So she changes tone, how slimy.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.370
So, let's go home.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:55.660
Yeah, let's go.

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:01.080
Sicil? There was a phone call?

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.290
I-It was from a friend.

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:07.590
I see. I'm going to go see Naozumi now.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:10.880
Mama has some music to talk about, so we'll go out.

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:13.680
The three of us will go to a restaurant tonight.

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:16.680
We're planning to go somewhere that has tasty desserts.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.560
Thank you.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:19.690
See ya.

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.690
I have to say it.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:28.190
I have to tell Papa now.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:30.360
"Naozumi and the others are going home to Japan."

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:33.070
I have to say it!

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:36.660
I have to say it now!

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.460
I'm sorry, Naozumi.

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:47.170
I'm sorry, Papa.

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:51.130
But I'm... I'm afraid!

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:54.470
Bernie.

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:56.470
I can't say goodbye.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:58.180
I might still see you again someday.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.480
Yeah, we'll see you again soon, right?

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.480
Take care, Bernie.

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:03.770
Take care!

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.270
I'll be fine.

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:10.690
We're all Japanese!

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:12.990
I'm from Japan, too!

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:16.990
Have you seen the movie about the rich driver?

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:19.580
The male star didn't come to New York.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:22.080
After that...

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:28.590
Bernie!

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:30.460
See ya later!

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:37.680
Sana! Naozumi! Rei!
See ya later!

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:41.390
Don't lean out the window of a running car or you'll hit your head.

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:43.350
Bye-bye. New York

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:42.770
Oh, dangerous!

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:48.190
Really, a very cool city...

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:50.280
Broadway.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:58.370
- It's not important anymore.
- Not important.

00:16:58.370 --> 00:16:59.580
He's called the Master...

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:01.580
Who's this Master?

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:05.790
Why are you looking at me all of a sudden?!

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:06.880
Dork.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:09.590
This place is Gary-san's office.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:12.800
First of all, Gary-san's secretary is asking for today's schedule.

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:16.680
Hey, brother! Here, Michelle-san is talking to the composer.

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:18.760
Very cool recording studio!

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:21.680
And what is Sicil-chan doing at this moment?

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:23.270
Ah, sorry!

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:27.480
Naozumi-kun and the others are on their way to the airport now.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.980
I was thinking of having us all live together.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:36.490
If I don't tell him, they'll go back to Japan.

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:39.160
Naozumi and the others decided to go home.

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:41.660
Then, Papa will give them up for sure.

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:46.670
Gary-san, Michelle-san, and you, Sicil, are all very important to me.

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:49.670
I love you more than anybody.

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:52.670
Please stop.

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.760
Naozumi said he was going home...

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:56.680
He decided that on his own...

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:09.690
Look, isn't it a shame?

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:11.770
We'll have to say good-bye to Manhattan at last.

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:14.480
Bye-bye, Manhattan!

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:17.570
Even though I'm a year-round driver,
I've never seen the Manhattan airport.

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:19.660
So I don't even know how to get there!

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:22.280
I'm kidding, don't worry...

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:26.160
That's a lie...

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:47.270
- Bye-bye, New York!
- People usually say this in foreign languages.

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:48.560
Usually Sana-chan says this!

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:52.310
I'm sorry, Naozumi.

00:18:57.190 --> 00:19:02.160
But I still don't want you to go... no...

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:07.160
What a nice car!

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:09.080
Oh no, I'm going to be late!

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:32.400
They're not there?

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:34.770
If you're looking for the people staying there, they've left.

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:37.280
They left? To where?

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:40.990
How would I know?
I was busy cleaning!

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:42.780
They already moved out anyway.

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:45.120
What does this mean, Naozumi?

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.290
We can see the airport!

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.880
Brad! Brad!

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:01.380
Please hurry! We have to catch Naozumi!

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:03.390
I gotcha! Hold on tight!

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:09.390
And you are...?

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:10.680
It's me.

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:14.400
Ah, Maeda-san. You're here early.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:15.690
Maeda-san?!

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:17.190
Maeda-san is this person!

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.780
Yeah.

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:21.360
This is Maeda-san now.

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:23.490
I don't get what happened!

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:28.160
They had such good meals I couldn't resist!

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.080
How sharp!

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:33.170
What's this? What's going on here?

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:35.960
Hold on tight!

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:38.670
This way!

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:42.380
Maeda-san looks like a bodyguard!
Oh yeah, we should check in the luggage...

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:46.760
We've invited Director of Musicals Hamilton to this program.

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:49.680
Ah, Gary! You're busy preparing now...

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:50.890
So, thank you for coming today!

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:54.270
This time, we're planning a big surprise for everybody!

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:58.690
Up till now, nobody has seen this musical.

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:02.070
When you see it, you'll definitely want to see it again!

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:05.200
Great, Gary!
We're waiting to enjoy it!

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.660
Let's go, Naozumi-kun.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:07.370
Okay.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.660
Sana-chan, Naozumi-kun,
we'll be leaving soon.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:11.790
I hope it'll be a pleasant ride.

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:13.160
Shall we go back? To Japan?

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:14.960
Yeah. Let's go home.

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:19.960
But what did you think of our trip to America?

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.170
No way.

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:28.800
Naozumi.

00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:33.680
They went back to Japan?!

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:35.770
They're probably already gone.

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:37.060
Why did this happen?

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:38.270
"Why"?!

00:21:38.270 --> 00:21:40.070
To tell the truth, it's because of your mistake.

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:42.070
It really hurt the boy.

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:45.360
I was put in charge of these.

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:47.700
It's because they couldn't get in touch with you.

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:50.660
Rei, Sana, and Naozumi wrote these letters.

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:53.660
Inside, they explained why they went back so suddenly.

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:55.790
You'll understand better from these.

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:58.670
Thank you.
Excuse me for interrupting your job.

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:04.170
Dumb old man.

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:08.090
It's going to be lonely around here.

00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:09.590
Ah, welc-

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:10.680
Hi, Bernie!

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:13.180
Is there an available apartment?

00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:21.570
Well, let's do this.

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:24.190
Yep, yep. The solution is not to leave.

00:22:24.190 --> 00:22:25.570
Let's go, Sana-chan.

00:22:25.570 --> 00:22:26.990
Let's go, Nao-Nao.

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:28.490
N... Nao-Nao?

00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:30.570
I feel so full of energy!

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:32.080
Let's go together...

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:34.080
It's all up to us!

